{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd; cat .agents/skills/noodle/SKILL.md; cat /Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/p-consumer-selection.json'","aggregated_output":"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle78-delivery-20260916/control/.worktrees/issue84-control/.worktrees/noodle-84-0-execute\n---\nname: noodle\ndescription: >-\n  Operate the Noodle CLI — explain commands, find flags, create/edit .noodle.toml config.\n  Also covers writing skills for Noodle: the orders pipeline, task-type schedule fields,\n  stage composition, and the orders-next.json schema. Use when running noodle commands,\n  editing .noodle.toml, writing or updating a skill's schedule field, or authoring new\n  task-type skills.\n---\n\n# Noodle\n\nSkills that run themselves. Write skills with a `schedule:` field describing when they should run. Noodle's scheduler agent reads those descriptions, writes orders, and the loop spawns agents in isolated worktrees to do the work.\n\n## How the Loop Works\n\n1. **Brief** — Noodle gathers project state into `.noodle/mise.json` (backlog, active agents, history, capacity, registered skills)\n2. **Schedule** — the scheduler agent reads mise, writes `.noodle/orders-next.json`\n3. **Dispatch** — Noodle promotes orders and spawns agent sessions\n4. **Execute** — each agent runs in its own worktree with the assigned skill\n5. **Merge** — completed work merges back to main\n\n## Skills\n\nA skill is a directory with a `SKILL.md`. The body is the agent's instructions. The frontmatter is metadata.\n\n**General skills** (no `schedule:`) are invoked directly by agents. Examples: `commit`, `debugging`.\n\n**Scheduled skills** (with `schedule:`) run autonomously. The scheduler reads the `schedule:` value as prose and uses judgment to decide when conditions are met.\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: quality\ndescription: Post-cook quality gate.\nschedule: \"Follow-up stage after execute. Cross-provider review preferred.\"\n---\n```\n\nSkills live in `.agents/skills/` by default. Paths in `skills.paths` are searched in order; first match wins.\n\nFor the full guide on writing skills, orders, and schedule fields, see [references/skill-authoring.md](references/skill-authoring.md).\n\n## Configuration\n\nNoodle reads `.noodle.toml` at project root. Scaffolded on first `noodle start`. Most projects only need:\n\n```toml\nmode = \"supervised\"  # auto | supervised | manual\n\n[routing.defaults]\nprovider = \"claude\"\nmodel = \"claude-opus-4-6\"\n\n[skills]\npaths = [\".agents/skills\"]\n```\n\nFull config reference: https://poteto.github.io/noodle/reference/configuration\n\n## CLI\n\nAll commands accept `--project-dir` (default: current directory, env: `NOODLE_PROJECT_DIR`).\n\n### Core\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle start` | Start the noodle loop |\n| `noodle start --once` | Run one scheduling cycle and exit |\n| `noodle status` | Show runtime status (active agents, queue depth, loop state) |\n| `noodle reset` | Clear all runtime state (refuses if loop is running) |\n\n### Initial proposal recovery (P-class)\n\nUse the existing Noodle owner with a known project and a stopped loop.\nRun noodle --project-dir <known-project> admission inspect and consume its JSON.\nFor recoverable, execute next.argv exactly as an argv array. Never reconstruct\nthe digest, revision or command from memory or a historical checkpoint.\nFor refused, preserve evidence and report next.required to next.provided_by.\nAfter that owner resolves the condition, use next.readback_argv to inspect again.\nA valid initial proposal remains available for normal admission; do not retire it.\nFor retired, follow next.argv once for fresh canonical readback. For no_proposal,\nrecovery is finished: next.argv is empty and next names the scheduling owner\nand inputs for a separately admitted intent. Do not loop inspection indefinitely.\nRetirement does not dispatch, restart, complete an order or authorize provider\nwrites. Record the actual JSON, argv and operation results. Missing owner/project\ninputs must be supplied by the supervising operator, not guessed by the Session.\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| noodle admission inspect | Inspect owner, subject, revision, invalid and exact next argv |\n| noodle admission retire PROPOSAL_SHA256 CURRENT_ORDER_REVISION | Archive and retire only the unchanged rejected initial proposal |\n\n### Skills & Schemas\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle skills` | List resolved skills |\n| `noodle skills list` | List all resolved skills |\n| `noodle schema <target>` | Print schema docs for a target |\n| `noodle schema list` | List available schema targets (`mise`, `orders`, `status`) |\n\n### Worktrees\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle worktree create <name>` | Create a new linked worktree |\n| `noodle worktree create <name> --from <ref>` | Create from a specific branch or commit |\n| `noodle worktree exec <name> <command...>` | Run a command inside a worktree (CWD-safe) |\n| `noodle worktree merge <name>` | Merge a worktree branch into integration branch |\n| `noodle worktree merge <name> --into <branch>` | Merge into a specific target branch |\n| `noodle worktree list` | List all worktrees with merge status |\n| `noodle worktree prune` | Remove merged and patch-equivalent worktrees |\n| `noodle worktree cleanup <name>` | Remove a worktree without merging |\n| `noodle worktree cleanup <name> --force` | Remove even with unmerged commits |\n| `noodle worktree hook` | Run worktree session hook (used internally) |\n\n### Events\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| `noodle event emit <type>` | Emit an external event into the loop |\n| `noodle event emit <type> --payload <json>` | Emit with a JSON payload |\n| `noodle event emit <type> --session <id>` | Emit to a specific session's event log |\n\nFull CLI reference: https://poteto.github.io/noodle/reference/cli\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n1. **\"fatal config diagnostics prevent start\"** — Check `.noodle.toml` against `noodle schema`.\n2. **Missing adapter scripts** — Create scripts or update paths in config.\n3. **Stale worktrees** — `noodle worktree list`, then `noodle worktree prune`.\n\n## References\n\n- [references/skill-authoring.md](references/skill-authoring.md) — writing skills: pipeline, orders schema, schedule fields, stage composition, full examples\n- [references/configuration.md](references/configuration.md) — full .noodle.toml config reference\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/adapters — adapter setup, script contracts, provider examples\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/scheduling — how the loop schedules and dispatches work\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/skills — skill discovery, composition, scheduled vs general\n- https://poteto.github.io/noodle/concepts/runtimes — process, sprites, and runtime routing\n{\n  \"binary\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle78-delivery-20260916/control/.worktrees/issue84-control/.worktrees/noodle-84-0-execute/bin/noodle\",\n  \"binary_sha256\": \"85bd747fc7f408844b1c61199fa36a7b7e96cb02ffe9ac502e33fd9ca88e6919\",\n  \"skill\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle78-delivery-20260916/control/.worktrees/issue84-control/.worktrees/noodle-84-0-execute/.agents/skills/noodle/SKILL.md\",\n  \"skill_sha256\": \"0dda11c1b839400686168505ce56cdd359e595ea78b9129a2761243959c496d0\",\n  \"cases\": {\n    \"stale-proposal\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/p-consumer-fixtures/stale-proposal\",\n    \"valid-proposal\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/p-consumer-fixtures/valid-proposal\"\n  },\n  \"prompt_sha256\": \"c682e16f953572ac9d4ce0aceed25d73926c8820db0e1560d9df97e101609e79\",\n  \"selected_at\": 1789629848.8774898,\n  \"carrier\": \"native macOS Codex CLI fresh P consumer; disposable fixtures\",\n  \"authorizes_landing\": false\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,hashlib,pathlib,platform,os,subprocess,time\nbase=pathlib.Path('/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917')\nselection=base/'p-consumer-selection.json'\njournal=base/'p-consumer-journal.json'\ns=json.loads(selection.read_text())\nj={'selection_path':str(selection),'started_at':time.time(),'carrier':platform.platform(),'calls':[],'statuses':[]}\ndef save(): journal.write_text(json.dumps(j,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nsave()\ntry:\n assert platform.system()=='Darwin','selected carrier requires native macOS'\n cwd=pathlib.Path.cwd().resolve()\n skill=(cwd/'.agents/skills/noodle/SKILL.md').resolve(strict=True)\n assert pathlib.Path(s['skill']).resolve(strict=True)==skill,'selected skill does not match current worktree'\n j['skill']={'resolved_path':str(skill),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(skill.read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\n assert j['skill']['sha256']==s['skill_sha256'],'skill digest mismatch'\n binary=pathlib.Path(s['binary']).resolve(strict=True)\n assert binary==cwd/'bin/noodle','selected binary is outside current worktree bin'\n assert binary.is_file() and os.access(binary,os.X_OK),'selected binary is not executable'\n j['binary']={'resolved_path':str(binary),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(binary.read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\n assert j['binary']['sha256']==s['binary_sha256'],'binary digest mismatch'\n assert set(s['cases'])=={'stale-proposal','valid-proposal'},'unexpected fixture cases'\n fixture_parent=(base/'p-consumer-fixtures').resolve(strict=True)\n j['fixtures']={}\n for name,p in s['cases'].items():\n  root=pathlib.Path(p).resolve(strict=True)\n  assert root==fixture_parent/name and root.is_dir(),'fixture root mismatch: '+name\n  runtime=root/'.noodle'\n  assert runtime.is_dir() and runtime.resolve(strict=True).is_relative_to(root),'runtime escapes fixture: '+name\n  j['fixtures'][name]=str(root)\n assert len(set(j['fixtures'].values()))==2,'fixtures are not distinct'\n j['statuses'].append('Validated native macOS carrier, selected binary and skill digests, and distinct disposable fixture roots.')\n save()\n argv=[str(binary),'--project-dir',j['fixtures']['stale-proposal'],'admission','--help']\n result=subprocess.run(argv,capture_output=True,text=True,timeout=30)\n call={'argv':argv,'stdout':result.stdout,'stderr':result.stderr,'returncode':result.returncode}\n j['calls'].append(call);save();print(json.dumps(j,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\nexcept Exception as e:\n j['blocker']=str(e);save();raise\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
