ues()))==2,'fixtures are not distinct'\n j['statuses'].append('Validated native macOS carrier, selected binary and skill digests, and distinct disposable fixture roots.')\n save()\n argv=[str(binary),'--project-dir',j['fixtures']['stale-proposal'],'admission','--help']\n result=subprocess.run(argv,capture_output=True,text=True,timeout=30)\n call={'argv':argv,'stdout':result.stdout,'stderr':result.stderr,'returncode':result.returncode}\n j['calls'].append(call);save();print(json.dumps(j,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\nexcept Exception as e:\n j['blocker']=str(e);save();raise\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"selection_path\": \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/p-consumer-selection.json\",\n  \"started_at\": 1789629886.7809331,\n  \"carrier\": \"macOS-26.6.2-arm64-arm-64bit-Mach-O\",\n  \"calls\": [\n    {\n      \"argv\": [\n        \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle78-delivery-20260916/control/.worktrees/issue84-control/.worktrees/noodle-84-0-execute/bin/noodle\",\n        \"--project-dir\",\n        \"/Users/neon/.codex/experiments/noodle84-20260917/p-consumer-fixtures/stale-proposal\",\n        \"admission\",\n        \"--help\"\n      ],\n      \"stdout\": \"Use the existing Noodle owner with a known project and a stopped loop.\\nRun noodle --project-dir <known-project> admission inspect and consume its JSON.\\nFor recoverable, execute next.argv exactly as an argv array. Never reconstruct\\nthe digest, revision or command from memory or a historical checkpoint.\\nFor refused, preserve evidence and report next.required to next.provided_by.\\nAfter that owner resolves the condition, use next.readback_argv to inspect again.\\nA valid initial proposal remains available for normal admission; do not retire it.\\nFor retired, follow next.argv once for fresh canonical readback. For no_proposal,\\nrecovery is finished: next.argv is empty and next names the scheduling owner\\nand inputs for a separately admitted intent. Do not loop inspection indefinit